(:id "port/moo/vt/blobs" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/mootable/vtcells_test.go: TestMooVariableTableCells/blobs" "internal/codegen/mootable/vtcells_test.go: TestMooVariableTableCellsNegativeControl/save-id-count/blobs, TestMooVariableTableCellsNegativeControl/load-id-order/blobs" "internal/codegen/mootable/stringidentity_test.go: TestMooStringIdentity, TestMooStringIdentityNegativeControl") :tested-revision "b6b6093dfb837e45b4a15d4134a17caacedf07ae" :note "2026-11-03: The row's manifest instances load through the emitted table_load.moo and save back byte for byte with measure equal to length, its report lines equal reports.txt, and its Go-engine constructs round-trip; the save-id-count and load-id-order controls are each red on this row. PR #2744. 2026-11-09 STRICT-100: string identity re-pinned as a strict verdict against the Go reference engine (internal/tablewire Encode/Decode). Equal strings at every *string site save by value; two buffers of equal text write two node records, never one, and a *string slot holds a buffer that the save keys by name, never by bytes. One node named from two slots (blob_shared) reads with one blob_shared counted and refuses to save, plain and retaining; so does one buffer named from two slots; the shared row's copy saves the reference's detached bytes. The four gates (decoded, built, copy, shared) answer the reference's bytes or refusal. The control planting identity-by-content turns the decoded and built rows red; dropping the blob_shared refusal turns the shared rows red. Run on vision (Linux x86-64) under the pinned moo f60f0239, SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
